firefighters in siberia are battling  massive wildfires which have been  burning for weeks  and are now beginning to threaten major  cities in the region of yakutia  the blazes have been fueled for months  by extreme heat  which scientists say is a result of  climate change  russian officials are using aircraft to  fight fires  currently burning across an area of some  120 square kilometers  on the ground the situation is said to  be improving  but it's far from under control  as for today the wildfire situation  remains difficult  and we have an emergency situation in  the region  as of this morning there were 40 active  forest fires  officials have also called in hundreds  of explosive experts to make fire breaks  creating gaps in the trees and  undergrowth should contain the fires  [Applause]  officials are worried that the flames  could reach nearby cities  people in the regional capital yakutsk  have for days been doing their best to  deal with living in a city  shrouded in thick smoke  there's an unpleasant scratchy feeling  in the throat but what can we do  it's hard to breathe especially with a  mask and the weather's hot  the weather is certainly a factor with  daytime temperatures of up to 35 degrees  celsius  unusually hot for the northern russian  region
 

